  "How do I stop my PR from being merged too early?": {
    "question": "How do I stop my PR from being merged too early?",
    "answer": "To prevent your PR from being merged too early, ensure you follow these steps:\n\n- Reference any issues related to your PR, or issues that your PR may solve. [1]\n- Avoid creating overly large changes in a single commit. Instead, break your PR into multiple small, logical commits. This makes it easier for your PR to be reviewed. [1]\n- Comment on your own PR where you believe something may need further explanation. [1]\n- Be selective when assigning your PR with `/assign @<username>`. Assigning excessive reviewers will not yield a quicker PR review. [1]\n- If your PR is considered a \"Work in progress\" prefix the name with `WIP` or use the `/hold` command. This will prevent the PR from being merged till the `WIP` or hold is lifted. [1]",
    "status": "ok",
