  "How do I squash my commits?": {
    "question": "How do I squash my commits?",
    "answer": "To squash your commits, follow these steps:\n\n1. Start an interactive rebase:\n   ```\n   git rebase -i HEAD~3\n   ```\n   [2][3]\n\n2. In the interactive rebase interface, mark the commits you want to keep as `pick` and the ones you want to squash as `squash` or `s`. [2][3]\n\n3. Save and close the editor. Git will then combine the marked commits into a single commit. [2][3]\n\n4. Force push your branch to update the remote repository:\n   ```\n   git push --force\n   ```\n   [2][3]",
    "status": "ok",
