  "How can I combine several commits into one before merging?": {
    "question": "How can I combine several commits into one before merging?",
    "answer": "To combine several commits into one before merging, you should squash your commits. This can be done by performing an interactive rebase [1]. Here’s how:\n\n1. Check your git branch:\n   ```\n   git status\n   ```\n\n2. Start an interactive rebase:\n   ```\n   git rebase -i HEAD~N\n   ```\n   Replace `N` with the number of commits you want to squash.\n\nBy squashing, you can create a single commit that represents a logical change, making the PR easier to review [1][2].",
