  "What are the requirements to become a Kubernetes org member?": {
    "question": "What are the requirements to become a Kubernetes org member?",
    "answer": "To become a Kubernetes org member, the following requirements must be met:\n\n- Have 2FA enabled on their GitHub account [1].\n- Join the k-dev mailing list [1].\n- List their active contributions, which should be significant enough to warrant membership [1].\n- List the active subprojects they are involved in [1].\n- Be sponsored by an existing member who meets the sponsor requirements [1][3].\n\nThe sponsor requirements include:\n\n- Being a member of the org they are attempting to sponsor for [3].\n- Having close interactions with the prospective member [3].\n- Being a reviewer or approver in at least one OWNERS file within one of the Kubernetes GitHub organizations [3].\n- Being from multiple member companies to demonstrate integration across the community [3].\n\nAdditionally, the process involves:\n\n- Opening an issue against the kubernetes/org repo and ensuring sponsors are @mentioned [3].\n- Completing every item on the checklist in the issue template [3].\n- Having sponsoring reviewers reply with a `+1` confirmation [3].\n- The request being reviewed by the Kubernetes GitHub Admin team [3].",
